Z||000000||Seanh||06-02-2001||09:15 AM||||Hey, I just bought a '81 Porsche 924, 5 spd, non-turbo. Anyway, it runs good, nothing like the Fiero, but I still like it. (BTW, I got it for $100, the hood had flown up while driving and the repair costs were more then he was selling it for so I told him I would give him $100 for it and he took it). The problem it has is, sometimes it doesn't like to start. It just cranks. If I floor the pedal it starts right up. This is a FI engine, so what could be the problem? Anyone know where I could find any information on this car on the net? Or a place that sells parts for it? It needs new seats, windshield, hood, and brakes. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||TRiAD||06-02-2001||11:24 AM||||Those cars were built by VW (as were the 944s), and had at one time a small cult-following. <BR>Searching on the net, you should be able to find a forum like this one dedicated to the front-engined 9s. <P>Good luck!<P>------------------<BR><B><I>Looking for a white '88 GT 5 sp...<BR>...Could it be...Found?<BR>Stay tuned!</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000002||firstfiero||06-02-2001||03:09 PM||||   had one....loved it. Their is a web site dedicated to just 924's. <A HREF="http://www.924.org/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.924.org/</A> <BR>Try this site...these guys our pretty knowledgeable. I found it when I was looking for another one to buy.I bought a fiero instead. Parts just to damn expensive for the 924.  have fun and if you want to sell it give me a call!<P>------------------<BR>Hey Mr. Ricer come over here and tell me how your stickers make you faster.....<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headshot.gif">         <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||thomas_l||06-03-2001||10:22 AM||||If it has Bosch CIS F/I like most early '80s Euro cars, they have kind of a hinkey cold start setup. On top of that, you really need to invest in the special fuel pressure testing setup (two lines with a valve and assorted banjo fittings. If you do any work on it yourself. Best just buy a good service manual and start on page 1.<P>Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierohoho||06-03-2001||08:16 PM||||Sounds like a good vehicle for a 2.8L engine swap.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
